      <PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>The organizations mission is to further cooperation and understanding between national groups in the United States. It exposes the public to the multitude of cultures represented by the member houses that belong to the House of Pacific Relations in Balboa Park in the City of San Diego, CA.</PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Sponsors a cultural and educational service organization for young members of the Houses. The HPR Queens Organization fosters a spirit of understanding, tolerance and goodwill between all races and nationalities, and prepares its members to be adult members of their International Houses. The Queens act as "goodwill ambassadors" of HPR and represent the music and dance of various ethnic groups at the events throughout San Diego County</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
        <ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>13414</ProgramServiceExpensesAmt>
      </ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>Sponsor major festivals including ethnic food fair that features food, drink and entertainment from all of the national groups. The international cottages also participate in Balboa Park December Nights with food and festivities inspired by winter holidays from around the world. The international houses are also open weekends throughout the year to educate the public.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
